  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Boeing obligated $5.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Boeing won 510 awards so far, with an average award size of $11.6M, and obligations are up 35.8% year over year. The Department of Defense is the single largest buyer, accounting for $5.9B of obligations in FY2026 to date. Aircraft Manufacturing is the dominant market, with $5.9B in obligations, while the next-largest market is Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $63.8M. Historical year-by-year obligations show variation: FY21 was $7.3B, FY22 was $3.9B, FY23 was $3.3B, FY24 was $5B, FY25 was $4.4B, and FY26 is $5.9B. The data are contract obligations except where award-value figures are specifically noted as total contract values in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables. This snapshot covers fiscal-year-to-date activity for FY2026 and does not represent a full fiscal year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Boeing's federal contracting trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations peaked at $7.3B in FY21 then dropped to $3.9B in FY22 and $3.3B in FY23. Obligations recovered to $5B in FY24, dipped to $4.4B in FY25, and rose to $5.9B in FY26 to date. FY2026 obligations are up 35.8% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Boeing's main federal buyers and what markets do they buy?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer, accounting for $5.9B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Aircraft Manufacturing is the top market at $5.9B, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $63.8M and Computer Systems Design Services at $14.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Boeing make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Boeing obligated $5.9B from federal contracts in FY2026 to date, on 510 awards with an average award size of $11.6M, and obligations are up 35.8% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Boeing?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense buys from Boeing, accounting for $5.9B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration shows $0 in obligations for Boeing in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Boeing sell to the government?",
      "a": "Boeing sells Aircraft Manufacturing to the government, accounting for $5.9B in FY2026 to date. Boeing also sells Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing ($63.8M), Computer Systems Design Services ($14.4M), and Engineering Services ($6.5M), among smaller markets."
    },
